#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""my-audio -- set the macOS default audio output by rules, and show the audio status.

A rule says "when this device is present, play through that one": an HDMI
display is plugged in -> its own audio; a Bluetooth speaker connects -> a
Multi-Output Device. `my-audio watch` (the LaunchAgent) applies the rules
each time the set of audio devices changes, and never in between -- so an
output chosen by hand stays until the next plug or unplug.

Standard library only: CoreAudio is called through ctypes.
"""
